Package: lsw
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: acceleration3 <acceleration23@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/acceleration3/linux-subsystem-windows
Depends: @SHLIBS@, libvirt-daemon, libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu, ovmf, qemu-utils, 7zip, curl, hicolor-icon-theme, libsdl3-0
Recommends: virtiofsd, pkexec, mesa-vulkan-drivers | vulkan-icd
Suggests: mesa-opencl-icd | opencl-icd, libegl-mesa0
Description: Linux Subsystem for Windows
 Windows applications as native windows, from a KVM guest with a
 paravirtual GPU that runs the guest's Direct3D, Vulkan, OpenGL and
 OpenCL on the host GPU. LSW sets up the Windows guest itself, under the
 user's own libvirt session (qemu:///session), and carries the patched
 QEMU, DXVK and vkd3d-proton it needs.
 .
 libvirt-daemon and its QEMU driver are the session daemon LSW's VMs
 run under, ovmf the UEFI firmware they boot, qemu-utils the disk tool;
 7zip reads the install media. SDL3 is loaded, not linked: DXVK's native
 build opens its window-system backend at start. virtiofsd serves shared
 folders, pkexec asks the one password that lets a USB device be passed
 to the guest, and OpenCL in the guest needs an OpenCL driver on the
 host.
